    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [X] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [X] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n- [X] I have updated 'mini.nvim' to latest version\n\n### Module(s)\n\nmini.pairs\n\n### Description\n\nSlightly laggy pairing on large files\n\n### Neovim version\n\nNVIM v0.9.0-dev-626+g42afa0369\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\nminimal.lua:\r\n```lua\r\nrequire('mini.pairs').setup {}\r\n```\r\n\r\n1. `nvim -nu minimal.lua`\r\n2. Open up a large file, like [this one](https://git.suckless.org/dwm/file/dwm.c.html)\r\n3. Go to a random line\r\n4. Begin typing pairs\r\n\n\n### Expected behavior\n\nInstantaneous pairing\n\n### Actual behavior\n\nFirst off, I love your plugins. Your work is great.\r\n\r\nNow I hate to make comparisons, but in my experience [nvim-autopairs](https://github.com/windwp/nvim-autopairs) just has mini.pairs beat in this regard. While I really want to use mini.pairs as I adore the minimal, non-bloated design of your plugins, there is a *slight* lag on large files that I just can't ignore. \r\n\r\nOn small files mini.pairs works instantaneously, but what I need from a pairing plugin is for it to do that all the time, no matter what.\r\n\r\nThen again, it is definitely possible I'm missing something. Let me know if you can replicate the issue.",
